# Vercel serves the mvp/ root. Without this, internal working files are publicly downloadable
# (e.g. /data/email_campaign.csv exposed ~5,700 reporters' raw emails + street addresses).
# Keep only what the deployed site actually needs: index.html, csr_profiles.js, graphics/.

# Backend scaffolding — NOT deployed (cost control). The api/ Stripe+Supabase functions +
# package.json trigger an npm install + serverless-function build on EVERY deploy, which was
# burning most of the build CPU minutes. The prototype doesn't need them: the only caller
# (claim -> api/connect/create-account) degrades to a demo fallback if the function 404s, and the
# functions can't work without real keys anyway. RE-INCLUDE these when actually wiring the backend
# (see docs/integration_checklist.md). Excluding them makes each deploy a static-file upload.
api/
package.json

# Reporter PII + working data (raw emails, addresses, campaign lists). NEVER deploy.
data/

# Internal strategy, pricing rationale, and marketing playbooks — not for the public.
docs/
marketing/

# Source + tooling (index.html is the built artifact; src/ is concatenated into it).
src/
scripts/
*.sh
README.md
prd-v1.rtf

# DB schema + env template (info leak; no reason to serve).
supabase/
.env.example
.claude/
